{%- doc -%}
  Builds the class list for a ../design-system/src/react/Button/Button.tsx button. Extracted from
  blocks/mionas-button.liquid so that block is not the only place the vocabulary is spelled out:
  blocks/mionas-add-to-cart.liquid needs the same classes on a <button> it cannot render itself, and
  used to rebuild the same `mionas-button--<variant>` string by hand -- two copies that had to be
  kept in step, and would silently diverge the moment a variant or size was added.

  IT EMITS CLASSES, NOT AN ELEMENT, and that is the most it can share. The add-to-cart button's
  markup has to come from snippets/add-to-cart-button.liquid: that snippet is the
  <add-to-cart-component> wrapper, the ref="addToCartButton" binding and the checkmark-burst spans
  that drive the added-to-cart animation and the fly-to-cart flight. There is nothing to parameterise
  there -- a shared element snippet would have to emit an <a>, a submit <button> and a
  quick-add <button> with on:click, which is three elements wearing one name.

  THE CSS THESE CLASSES NEED IS NOT DELIVERED BY THIS SNIPPET EITHER. It lives in
  snippets/mionas-button-styles.liquid, rendered once per page from snippets/design-system-bridge.liquid.
  It used to be a {% raw %}{% stylesheet %}{% endraw %} tag in blocks/mionas-button.liquid, which meant it only shipped on
  pages where that block actually rendered -- see that snippet's header for what broke.

  @param {string} [variant] - primary, secondary, outline, ghost, danger, inverse-primary or inverse-ghost. Anything else falls back to primary.
  @param {string} [size] - sm, md or lg. Defaults to md, which adds no modifier because .mionas-button carries the md metrics itself.
  @param {boolean} [full_width] - Adds the --full modifier.
  @param {string} [prefix] - Classes to put in front, for a caller's own hooks (e.g. add-to-cart-button, which Horizon's animation CSS hangs off).

  @example
  {%- capture button_classes -%}
    {%- render 'mionas-button-class', variant: 'primary', size: 'md', full_width: true -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  comment
    Whitelisted rather than interpolated: a snippet is reachable from anywhere, and an unrecognised
    value would emit a modifier class that no rule matches -- a button with the base metrics and no
    colour at all, which is harder to spot than an obviously wrong one. Same reasoning, and the same
    shape, as the role whitelist in snippets/mionas-text.liquid.

    Keep both lists in step with the rules in snippets/mionas-button-styles.liquid. The blocks'
    schemas may offer FEWER options than these -- blocks/mionas-add-to-cart.liquid deliberately
    exposes four of the seven variants, because danger and the inverse pair would only ever be
    misconfigurations on a white product card. That restriction belongs in the schema, not here.
  endcomment
  assign allowed_variants = 'primary|secondary|outline|ghost|danger|inverse-primary|inverse-ghost' | split: '|'
  assign resolved_variant = variant | default: 'primary'
  unless allowed_variants contains resolved_variant
    assign resolved_variant = 'primary'
  endunless

  assign allowed_sizes = 'sm|md|lg' | split: '|'
  assign resolved_size = size | default: 'md'
  unless allowed_sizes contains resolved_size
    assign resolved_size = 'md'
  endunless

  assign classes = 'mionas-button mionas-button--' | append: resolved_variant

  comment
    md adds no modifier: .mionas-button already carries the md height, padding and font-size, so a
    --md class would have nothing to declare.
  endcomment
  unless resolved_size == 'md'
    assign classes = classes | append: ' mionas-button--' | append: resolved_size
  endunless

  if full_width
    assign classes = classes | append: ' mionas-button--full'
  endif

  if prefix != blank
    assign classes = prefix | append: ' ' | append: classes
  endif
-%}
{{- classes -}}
